The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (S.len > 1) {
    if      (dir == LEFT  && S.dir == RIGHT)
        S.dir = RIGHT;
    else if (dir == RIGHT && S.dir == LEFT)
        S.dir = LEFT;
    else if (dir == UP    && S.dir == DOWN)
        S.dir = DOWN;
    else if (dir == DOWN  && S.dir == UP)
        S.dir = UP;
}
```
Reason:
The condition `if (S.len > 1)` restricts the snake from changing direction when its length is greater than 1, which is essential for proper gameplay. This leads to unintended behavior where the snake cannot navigate correctly, especially when trying to turn.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
else
    S.dir = dir;
```
Reason:
By adding the `else` statement to allow the direction to change regardless of the snake's length, the patch ensures that the snake can navigate properly and change direction even when its length is greater than 1, thus restoring expected gameplay behavior.

